  "term": "hemiamblyopia",
  "definition": "Hemiamblyopia is a partial dimming of vision affecting one half of the visual field rather than complete blindness. In the historical usage here, it refers to reduced responsiveness to objects on the side opposite a brain lesion, while central vision remains relatively better preserved.",
